    "summary": "At least ten people were injured on Sunday in Mogadishu's Yaaqshiid district when government forces clashed with residents resisting home demolitions in the Tookiyo neighborhood. The dispute highlights ongoing tensions over land ownership and forced evictions in the city.",
    "content": "At least ten people were injured on Sunday in the Yaaqshiid district of Mogadishu during a confrontation between government security forces and local residents. The violence occurred when authorities moved to demolish homes in the Tookiyo neighborhood, an area the federal government claims as state-owned land.\n\nResidents, who had been ordered to leave their homes, refused to comply and organized street protests to oppose the operation. The ensuing clash left nearly ten people wounded, according to local reports. The incident underscores the volatile nature of land disputes in the Somali capital.\n\nThe demolition in Tookiyo is the latest in a series of forced evictions that have intensified across Mogadishu over the past year. Many residents argue that they have lived on the land for generations and hold legitimate claims, while the government asserts its ownership and has vowed to reclaim public property. These operations have repeatedly sparked protests and clashes, exposing deep frustrations over housing and displacement.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom maintain close ties to relatives in Mogadishu, the incident raises concerns about the safety and stability of neighborhoods where they may own property or plan to return. The lack of clear land tenure and the risk of sudden demolition make investment in housing or businesses precarious, often discouraging diaspora contributions to local development. The latest clash in Tookiyo has also prompted calls for dialogue, with community leaders urging the government to halt demolitions until fair compensation and alternative housing arrangements are provided.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/08/23/clashes-in-mogadishus-tookiyo-leave-ten-hurt-over-demolitions/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=clashes-in-mogadishus-tookiyo-leave-ten-hurt-over-demolitions",
